WEBVTT

00:00:00.413 --> 00:00:02.106
<v><b>Speaker 1:</b></v> <b>The 13th century</b>

00:00:03.246 --> 00:00:06.186
Guns were invented by the Chinese.

00:00:06.539 --> 00:00:10.542
The first guns were quite large, like small cannons.

00:00:10.837 --> 00:00:16.305
The oldest gun that still exists today was made in about 1280.

00:00:17.353 --> 00:00:22.643
Glasses were invented by the Italians in about 1286.

00:00:23.089 --> 00:00:27.310
Sunglasses were invented even earlier, in the twelfth century.

00:00:29.348 --> 00:00:31.012
<v><b>Speaker 2:</b></v> <b>The 18th century</b>

00:00:32.227 --> 00:00:38.597
The hot-air balloon was invented by two French brothers, Joseph and Jacques Montgolfier.

00:00:39.200 --> 00:00:46.583
The first flight with people was in 1783, and the balloon flew three kilometres over Paris.

00:00:48.721 --> 00:00:50.412
<v><b>Speaker 1:</b></v> <b>The 19th century</b>

00:00:51.542 --> 00:00:55.813
Stamps were invented by an English teacher, Rowland Hill.

00:00:56.558 --> 00:01:01.122
The first stamp, from 1840, was called the Penny Black,

00:01:01.259 --> 00:01:04.368
and it showed the head of the young Queen Victoria.

00:01:05.428 --> 00:01:10.905
The saxophone was invented by a Belgian musician in 1846.

00:01:11.276 --> 00:01:13.532
His name was Adolphe Sax.

00:01:13.807 --> 00:01:17.988
Saxophones were first used mainly in military bands,

00:01:18.065 --> 00:01:20.937
but are now used in all kinds of music.

00:01:23.032 --> 00:01:24.722
<v><b>Speaker 2:</b></v> <b>The 20th century</b>

00:01:25.643 --> 00:01:32.396
The biro was invented in the 1930s by a Hungarian journalist, Laszlo Biro.

00:01:33.125 --> 00:01:38.894
His invention was successful because the ink from the pen dried very quickly on paper.

00:01:39.885 --> 00:01:47.238
In 1943, Biro moved to Argentina because of the war in Germany, and he died there.

00:01:47.990 --> 00:01:53.125
The word ‘biro’ is now the most used name for any ballpoint pen.

00:01:54.241 --> 00:02:01.247
Lego was invented in 1932 by a Danish businessman, Ole Kirk Christiansen.

00:02:01.734 --> 00:02:08.887
The name <i>Lego</i> comes from the Danish phrase <i>leg godt</i>, which means ‘play well’.

00:02:09.775 --> 00:02:13.705
Twenty billion pieces of Lego are produced every year.

00:02:15.019 --> 00:02:20.523
CDs were invented by a Dutch company, Philips, in 1970.

00:02:21.305 --> 00:02:27.410
Sony also worked on CDs, and they were designed to play 74 minutes of music

00:02:27.639 --> 00:02:34.000
because that was the length of Beethoven’s <i>Ninth Symphony</i> – the Sony boss’s favourite piece of music.

00:02:35.098 --> 00:02:38.465
The mobile phone was invented by an American company.

00:02:39.031 --> 00:02:42.177
It was first produced by the company Motorola.

00:02:43.050 --> 00:02:47.304
On 3rd April 1973, Martin Cooper,

00:02:47.627 --> 00:02:52.723
a Motorola researcher and executive, made the first mobile telephone call.

00:02:53.373 --> 00:02:57.008
His phone weighed one point one kilograms.

00:02:59.156 --> 00:03:00.982
<v><b>Speaker 1:</b></v> <b>The 21st century</b>

00:03:01.815 --> 00:03:08.179
The virtual assistant Siri was invented by three American engineers in 2010.

00:03:08.500 --> 00:03:12.837
They later sold it to Apple for $200 million dollars.

00:03:13.230 --> 00:03:16.473
It speaks, recognizes voice commands,

00:03:16.530 --> 00:03:22.357
and can do things like answer questions, turn things on and off, and pay bills.

00:03:22.931 --> 00:03:28.401
The voice of Siri is provided by different actors in different countries and,

00:03:28.475 --> 00:03:31.491
in addition to male and female voices,

00:03:31.588 --> 00:03:37.468
in 2022 Apple added a gender-neutral voice option called Quinn.